<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Cast campaign, lever `fieldtype`: a synthesized record's field that some
    access holds as a pointer is declared as that pointer.

    structsynth types a field from the widest access it measured, and among
    accesses of one width the first it meets decides. At -O0 a field is
    reloaded for every use, so the first load of a buffer field is the one an
    integer add reads, and the field is declared int8 although the next load
    hands it to memmove. Every pointer use then prints a cast back:

        memmove((void *)a0->field_0x0,(void *)(a0->field_0x0 + (a0->field_0x8 - a0->field_0x10)),a0->field_0x10);

    Stage / sub-stage: P5 "aggregate-union". The P0 assertion
    `option fieldtype on|off` decides whether structsynth declares such a field
    as the most specific pointer its accesses prove: a value dereferenced,
    called, handed to a declared pointer parameter or returned by a function
    declared to return one. A type a value picks up by being merged with
    another value is not proof, and a field some access divides, shifts,
    multiplies or compares with sign stays a number.

    The fixture is decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/fieldtype_x86_64.c.
    Built by gcc -O0:

        buf_shift:   sort's fillbuf - the buffer is added to, then handed to
                     memmove; it becomes the void * memmove proves (the char *
                     the loop walks reaches it only through the loop's phi)
        ent_release: ls's free_ent - a context compared with a sentinel, then
                     handed to strlen and free
        ops_run:     a function-pointer field compared with zero, then called
        range_walk:  sort's mergelines_node - two walking pointers and the two
                     end pointers nothing but the loop test compares them with;
                     the end pointers take the walking pointers' type. The
                     pointer differences cast both sides back to an integer,
                     the price of the right type
        cell_val:    a control - a union member read as a double and as a
                     pointer stays raw bytes in both passes
        slot_post:   a control - an index read at a table, then handed to
                     write as its buffer, stays a number in both passes

    Built by clang -O2, with `option operand_refs on` so the "NULL" constant is
    a string as the CLI's default mode makes it:

        pctx_print:  a control, e2fsck's expand_percent_expression - the number
                     is compared first, then every case sinks into one fprintf,
                     so the number and the string reach it through one register
                     typed char *. The number stays a number in both passes

    Pass 1 (`option fieldtype off`, the default) reproduces the casts and pass 2
    (`option fieldtype on`) is the fix.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
