<stringmatch name="fieldtype #1: with the option off the buffer is an integer and memmove gets it through two casts - the bug" min="1" max="1">memmove\(\(void \*\)a0->field_0x0,\(void \*\)\(a0->field_0x0 \+ \(a0->field_0x8 - a0->field_0x10\)\),a0->field_0x10\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #2: with the option on the buffer is the void * memmove proves and memmove takes it as it is" min="1" max="1">memmove\(a0->field_0x0,\(void \*\)\(\(int8\)a0->field_0x0 \+ \(a0->field_0x8 - a0->field_0x10\)\),a0->field_0x10\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #3: with the option on the loop takes the buffer as it is, and indexes it as the char * it walks" min="1" max="1">for \(v1 = a0->field_0x0; v1 [&lt;] &amp;\(\(char \*\)a0->field_0x0\)\[a0->field_0x8\]; v1 = &amp;v1\[1\]\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #4: with the option off strlen gets the context through a cast" min="1" max="1">v2 = strlen\(\(char \*\)a0->field_0x10\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #5: with the option on the context is the char * strlen takes" min="1" max="1">v2 = strlen\(a0->field_0x10\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #6: with the option off the function pointer is called through a cast" min="1" max="1">v1 = \(\*\(code \*\)a0->field_0x8\)\(a0->field_0x10\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #7: with the option on the function pointer is called as it is" min="1" max="1">v1 = \(\*a0->field_0x8\)\(a0->field_0x10\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #8: with the option off the walking pointers are dereferenced through casts" min="1" max="1">v1 = v1 \* 7 \+ \(\*\(int8 \*\)a0->field_0x0 - \*\(int8 \*\)a0->field_0x8\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #9: with the option on they are dereferenced and stepped as pointers" min="1" max="1">a0->field_0x8 = &amp;a0->field_0x8\[-1\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #10: the end pointers take the walking pointers' type, so the loop test needs no cast in either pass" min="2" max="2">while \(\(a0->field_0x0 != a0->field_0x10 &amp;&amp; \(a0->field_0x8 != a0->field_0x18\)\)\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #11: a union member read as a double and as a pointer stays raw bytes in both passes" min="2" max="2">v2 = \*\(float8 \*\)a0->field_0x8;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #12: an index read at a table and handed to write stays a number in both passes, so write gets it through a cast" min="2" max="2">v3 = \(void \*\)a1->field_0x8;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="fieldtype #13: a number merged with a string on its way to fprintf stays a number in both passes" min="4" max="4">v1 = \(char \*\)a3->field_0x0;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
